# Build outputs that a web deploy has no use for.
#
# Without this the upload is ~580 MB, nearly all of it Scarb and Noir
# artifacts: cairo/target is 168 MB, cairo-verifier/target 111 MB, and each
# generated Honk verifier carries another ~86 MB. None of it is read by
# `next build`.
#
# The pattern is one level deep on purpose. `circuits/*/target` matches
# circuits/shuffle_open_verifier/target and NOT
# circuits/shuffle_open_verifier/example_proof/beta16_build/target -- which
# must be uploaded, because scripts/build_client_circuits.mjs stages the three
# compiled circuits from there into public/circuits/ during the build. A blunt
# `**/target` would exclude those too and the deployed app would serve no
# circuits at all: it would load, connect, read a table, and fail on the first
# shuffle with a 404.
cairo/target
cairo-verifier/target
circuits/*/target

# Cairo test/build caches and local records.
cairo/.snfoundry_cache
cairo-verifier/.snfoundry_cache
circuits/*/.snfoundry_cache
